## Lesson shape (typical)

`slug`, `title`, `summary`, `duration`, `whyItMatters`, `sections[]` (`heading`, `body`, `bullets?`, `codeExample?`), `checklist[]`, `pitfalls[]`, `interviewPrompts[]`, `diagram|null`, `related[]`. Optional: `likelyAnswerPoints`, `practiceMode`, `runtimeTarget`, `questionHighlights`, `questionBank`, `exercises`, `interactive`. DSA/AI/HLD/LLD learning labs may use `exercises[]` with `starterCode`, `solution`, `hints`, and `expectedOutput` for in-page coding practice, plus `type: 'design'` drills where authored.

LLD lessons (all modules) are self-contained: 5+ long sections, multiple `codeExample` snippets, coding + design `exercises[]`, and interactive topic labs. Current authored LLD guidance emphasizes 5-10 minute prompt framing, a running happy path before elegance, thin ports/adapters seams, composition over inheritance, and evaluator-style review.

AI learning expansion lessons under `ml-interactive-lab` and `deep-learning-from-scratch` are self-contained concept lessons: 5-7 long sections per lesson, multiple `codeExample` snippets, and at least two runnable coding exercises. DSA learning expansion lessons under the five DSA labs follow the same density, include design drills, and frame OA vs phone vs onsite expectations.

AI core lessons (via enrichment) and AI expansion labs are self-contained: ≥5 long sections, multiple `codeExample` snippets, ≥2 runnable coding exercises using NumPy/pandas/matplotlib/scikit-learn only. Every AI lesson also has a topic lab in `interactiveLessons.js`.

HLD exhaustive labs (`data-storage-lab`, `security-operations-lab`, `distributed-systems-lab`) are self-contained: 6 long sections, multiple `codeExample`s, design + coding exercises, curated `likelyAnswerPoints`, interactive topic labs, deep dives, and module-specific simulation blueprints.

Ids: `{moduleSlug}/{lessonSlug}` via `normalizeModule()`.

## Deep knowledge (`lessonDeepKnowledge.js`)

- `getLessonDeepKnowledge(lessonId)` — curated deeper insights + external references per lesson
- Sources under `deepKnowledge/` including `learningExpansionDeepKnowledge.js` (spreads `hldExhaustiveLabDeepKnowledge.js` plus DSA pattern/essentials snippets), `aiAdvancedDeepKnowledge.js`, `aiIndustryDeepKnowledge2026.js`, and `lldAdvancedDeepKnowledge.js` for advanced + hot-path LLD lessons
- Each entry: `insights[]` (`heading`, `body`) and `references[]` (`title`, `url`, `source`, `note`)
- Loaded in lesson route (`+page.js`) and rendered in the lesson page **Deep dive** section

## Banks and extras

- Question JSON (lazy in `QuestionBankIDE`): `top-interview-questions-*.json`, company files, strategy files — normalized by `src/lib/dsa/questionBank.js`
- DSA also pulls `all-companies-questions.json`, `leetcode-companies.json`
- DSA practice modules select highlights with chapter + title filters (`strictChapters`) so drills stay on-pattern for current company mixes
- `interactiveLessons.js` — merges expansion interactive maps, `aiInteractiveExtras`, 2026 AI currency overlays, and `lldInteractiveLabs.js`
- `_dsaEssentialsInteractiveSnippet.js` and `_dsaEssentialsDeepKnowledgeSnippet.js` — companion interactive/deep-dive records keyed by `dsa-interview-essentials-lab/{lesson}`
- Expansion lessons include on-page teaching sections, code examples, exercises, interactive topic labs, and deep-dive essays (not reference-only)
- `simulationLessons.js` — authored + generated HLD sims; module blueprints include the three exhaustive HLD lab modules
- `scripts/hld_lab_content.py` + `scripts/build_hld_exhaustive_labs.py` — author/regenerate exhaustive HLD lab payloads
- `lessonEnhancements.js` + `solutionLoader.js` — rich solutions for case studies
- Diagrams: `/primer-images/*` under `static/` (asserted in `tests/courseData.test.js`)
